{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Update README on SVG add",
  "description": "When a new SVG file is created in the workspace, automatically updates the README.md and public/index.html to include the new diagram.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": [
      "public/*.svg"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A new SVG file was just created in public/. Do the following:\n1. Update README.md: list all .svg files in the public/ directory and regenerate the full list under the \"## Diagrams\" section. Each entry should be `- [Project Name](./public/filename.svg)` where the project name is derived from the filename (remove .svg extension, replace hyphens/underscores with spaces, title case it).\n2. Update public/index.html: find the `const diagrams = [...]` array and add a new entry as `{ file: 'filename.svg', name: 'Project Name' }` where the name is derived from the filename (remove .svg, replace hyphens/underscores with spaces, title case)."
  }
}